Attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The idea this program implements — reading the quota an AI coding tool has
left on the machine you are sitting at, and putting it somewhere you can see
it — comes from CodexBar by Peter Steinberger:

    https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar
    MIT License, Copyright (c) Peter Steinberger

CodexBar is a macOS menu-bar application. subnsub-monitor is an independent
implementation in a different shape: a headless agent that dials out and
pushes to a relay, so a browser can watch a machine it has no route to. No
CodexBar source code is used or included here.

Credit follows the idea, not the source tree. CodexBar got there first.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Earlier releases (2026.08.15.x) could optionally install AgentsView
(https://github.com/kenn-io/agentsview, MIT License, Copyright (c) Kenn
Software LLC) as the per-machine session index behind the fleet search.
Since 2026.08.18 the search is implemented in this program itself and no
AgentsView code or binary is fetched, used, or included.
